motions.motion_text:
WHEREAS the City of Ottawa relies on specialized fleet equipment to undertake rural road maintenance, road-side grass cutting, ditching, gravel road grading, shoulder maintenance and other rural seasonal maintenance work;
WHEREAS Municipal Quality Standards (MQS) provide the standards for rural seasonal operations;
WHEREAS Ottawa's maintenance season is constrained by weather, making the availability of specialized fleet equipment essential to delivering planned work programs and maintaining infrastructure to meet the MQS;
WHEREAS Council has an interest in supporting efficient City operations where equipment is available when operationally needed and disruption during the active maintenance season is avoided or mitigated;
WHEREAS communication regarding planned maintenance and minimum standards provides councillors and residents with a means of assessing whether services are being adequately delivered.
THEREFORE BE IT RESOLVED that the Agriculture and Rural Affairs Committee recommend Council direct staff provide members of ARAC with a rural maintenance plan by  April 1st each year for the upcoming spring, summer, and fall seasons.
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that, for each stream of maintenance work (line-painting, road-side grass cutting, ditching, gravel road grading, shoulder maintenance) the plan include:
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that staff provide regular updates that can be shared with the public throughout the season on the implementation of the plan; and
BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED that staff meet with Members of ARAC by December 1steach year on the results of the plan, including whether the MQS was met for each stream and, where it was not met and/or where opportunities for improvement were observed, identify any changes needed to support achievement in the year ahead.
